Dragon Burst renut 0118: widescreen - the game's 2D placed by Burst Limit (wide_aspect.h), the frame shown at its shape

With aspect_ratio wider than 16:9 (auto = the screen's shape) Burst Limit v7.3 draws a wider view (hor+) into its
1280x720 frame. The Renut now asks the game where each 2D draw over the main target goes (the overlay placement
callback, PlaceOverlay in burstlimit_widescreen.cpp, as the PC's D3D12 path does) and moves its viewport and scissor;
the present shows the frame at rex::graphics::GetGuestDisplayAspect (stretched across) and records the surface size
for auto.

